<h2 class="doc-h2">Headings and motion</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The headline is an <code>h2</code> where upstream writes <code>h1</code>, because a section in a
    page sits under that page's own title; <code>HeadingLevel="1"</code> is for a page that is
    nothing but the FAQ. The finished section is in the markup, so a reader without scripting —
    or with <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> — gets it at once, without the entrance.
</p>
